prompts.handoff.index_context:
# Handoff notes

This conversation continues work that a previous conversation handed off when its context ran out. It left the notes below, and they are all that remains of it. Read them with read_handoff_note before you continue.

{notes}

prompts.host_notice.mcp_unavailable:
These MCP servers selected for this conversation could not be used at the start of this turn, so none of their tools are offered now:
{servers}

The other selected servers' tools are available as usual. If the task needs one of these servers, tell the user it is unavailable and why rather than working around it.

prompts.host_notice.preview_start_failed:
The user started {name} from the preview pane and it failed to start with this error:

{error}

If its entry in .mewrk/launch.json or the project is the cause, fix it and start it again with preview_start; otherwise tell the user what is wrong.

prompts.system.environment_section:
# Environment
You have been invoked in the following environment:
{facts}

prompts.system.hooks_section:
## Lifecycle hooks

Selected: {hook_names}
{hooks}

Hooks are run by the host's lifecycle, never by you; do not claim a hook succeeded unless a verifiable execution result appears in the context.

prompts.system.mcp_section:
## Selected MCP servers

{servers}

These entries come from the servers declared in the user's or a workspace's `.mewrk/mcp.json` and selected for this conversation. Their tools can be called only when the host exposed them to this turn; never claim a connection or an execution succeeded on the strength of this list alone.

prompts.system.skill_added_body:
## Skill added: {name}

This skill was selected after the conversation had already started, so its instructions arrive here rather than in the system prompt. They are in force from this point on, exactly as if they had been there all along.

{body}

