This tool runs bash — Git Bash on Windows, the system's own bash on macOS and Linux — never cmd.exe or PowerShell. Use Unix shell syntax: `/dev/null` not `NUL`, forward slashes, `$VAR` not `%VAR%` or `$env:VAR`. On macOS that bash is usually 3.2 with BSD tools unless a newer one is installed: bash 4 features (`mapfile`, `declare -A`, `${var,,}`) may be missing, and GNU-only flags differ (`sed -i ''`, not `sed -i`).

Each workspace keeps its own working directory between commands, on any machine; a command that ends outside its workspace sends the next one there back to the workspace root. Shell state does not persist: variables you export, functions you define, and `umask` are gone by the next call. The shell is initialized from your profile, so your own aliases and functions are available.

Output is captured as UTF-8 with CRLF folded to LF, and stdout is followed by stderr.{?find|grep|read|edit|write}

